Derivation
----------

`scripts/build_taxonomy.py` regenerates the file. It emits one row per
single-token noun lemma:

    lemma<TAB>ancestor1|ancestor2|...

Ancestors come from the hypernym closure of a single chosen sense — the synset
whose own name is the lemma, falling back to sense 1 — rather than from every
sense, because an all-senses closure produces false categories. Ancestors too
abstract to discriminate (`entity`, `abstraction`, `object`, …) are dropped.
